  - when useEffect called : when page render its get call

    - if no dependancy array => useEffect is called every render
    - if dependancy array is empty [] => useEffect is called on intial render (just once)
    - if dependancy array is there (not empty) => then it will called wheneer it changes

  - dont create useState inside your body component not the gloabl level and use useState on the top which leads to inconsistancy in program
  - dont create useState inside if/else , forloop and even inside function

  - routing in react

    - there are 2 types of routing

      - client side :
      - server side :

        - Client side :
          The browser loads a single HTML file along with a JavaScript bundle. Navigating between "pages" doesn’t involve fetching a new HTML file from the server. Instead, React dynamically updates the DOM to show different components based on the URL.

          - Tools:
            - The most common library is React Router (react-router-dom). You define routes such as /, /about, /contact that render specific components.

          Benefits:

          - Faster page transitions—no full reloads.
          - Smoother user experience, typical of single-page applications (SPAs).
          - Can implement dynamic/nested routes and control over navigation history.

  - lifecycle of class based component

    - constructor -> render
    - if componentDidMount and child component exists then
      - parent constructor-> parent render -> child constructor -> child render -> child componentDidmount -> parent componentDidMount
    - componentDidMount : used to make api call but why inside
      - API calls are made inside componentDidMount in class-based React components to ensure the API request happens after the component has been rendered and added to the DOM. This aligns with React's lifecycle: componentDidMount runs only once, immediately after the initial render, making it the ideal place for side effects such as data fetching.
    - check diagram : react lifecycle methods -diagram
    - classs based component require default value beccause we need to render with dummy data then on componentDidMount we can put exactly data

